From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_sync: check the command bit before reading the sync train parameters

The firmware of the MediaTek MT6897 sets the Synchronization Train bit on
page 2 of its LMP features, but it does not list Read Synchronization
Train Parameters among its supported commands and answers it with Unknown
HCI Command. The controller then fails to initialize.

Check the supported commands as well, like the other optional commands of
the same init stage.
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -4941,7 +4941,8 @@
 /* Check for Synchronization Train support */
 static int hci_read_sync_train_params_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
-	if (!lmp_sync_train_capable(hdev))
+	/* Read Synchronization Train Parameters is bit 7 of octet 31 */
+	if (!lmp_sync_train_capable(hdev) || !(hdev->commands[31] & 0x80))
 		return 0;
 
 	return __hci_cmd_sync_status(hdev, HCI_OP_READ_SYNC_TRAIN_PARAMS,
